WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.637
Which cloud you're in
matters here in a quiet way.

2
00:00:02.637 --> 00:00:07.500
Learn's incident samples ask you for the
cloud, but if they don't recognize your

3
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:12.363
answer, such as GCC, they fall back to
the worldwide endpoint without saying so.

4
00:00:12.363 --> 00:00:15.752
That's right for GCC by
accident: a typo isn't caught,

5
00:00:15.752 --> 00:00:19.388
and nothing records which
cloud the run was meant for.

6
00:00:19.388 --> 00:00:24.062
The chapter's code uses the same hosts
but refuses a cloud name it doesn't know.

7
00:00:24.062 --> 00:00:28.545
Graph's own rule evaluator is
a beta, delegated-only action,

8
00:00:28.545 --> 00:00:32.000
listed for the global
service, which GCC uses.

9
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.772
And the memberOf preview
is public cloud only,

10
00:00:34.772 --> 00:00:37.820
which is one more reason
the library doesn't use it.
